---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />

    <!-- Permanent Cache-Busting Network Headers for Clean Vercel Deployments -->
    <meta http-equiv="Cache-Control" content="no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate" />
    <meta http-equiv="Pragma" content="no-cache" />
    <meta http-equiv="Expires" content="0" />

    <title>[00] SOLOVERSE - CRAZY 8'S [TUTORIAL RULEBOOK] [START HERE]</title>
    <style>
        /* ==========================================================================
           1. COMPREHENSIVE SEMANTIC DESIGN TOKENS (LIGHT & DARK MODES)
           ========================================================================== */
        :root {
            /* Base Platform Architecture Tokens */
            --bg-main: #0f1015;
            --bg-card: #171922;
            --bg-main-box: #1c1e27;
            --text-primary: #ffffff;
            --text-secondary: #f3f4f6;
            --text-muted: #9ca3af;
            --text-divider: #2d313f;
            --color-link: #3b82f6;

            /* --- DARK MODE ELEMENT THEME TOKENS --- */
            /* Typography Accents */
            --color-card-title: #3b82f6;     /* Calibrated Blue for typography on dark */
            --color-card-class: #8cfffb;     /* Neon Light Blue */

            /* Callout Boxes (Background Opacities & Solid Structural Borders) */
            --border-tip: #aded8f;           /* Light Green */
            --bg-tip: rgba(173, 237, 143, 0.04);

            --border-note: #0ed145;          /* Green */
            --bg-note: rgba(14, 209, 69, 0.04);

            --border-example: #fff200;       /* Yellow */
            --bg-example: rgba(255, 242, 0, 0.04);

            --border-discards: #ff7f27;      /* Orange (Side & Top actions) */
            --bg-discards: rgba(255, 127, 39, 0.04);

            --border-challenge: #b97a56;     /* Light Brown */
            --bg-challenge: rgba(185, 122, 86, 0.04);

            --border-important: #a75e28;     /* Calibrated brighter Dark Brown for visibility */
            --bg-important: rgba(167, 94, 40, 0.04);

            --border-restriction: #ec1c24;   /* Red (Restriction & Penalty) */
            --bg-restriction: rgba(236, 28, 36, 0.04);

            --border-compatibility: #ffaec8; /* Pink */
            --bg-compatibility: rgba(255, 174, 200, 0.04);

            --border-victory: #b497ef;       /* Light Purple */
            --bg-victory: rgba(180, 151, 239, 0.04);

            --border-two-player: #9d00ff;    /* Purple */
            --bg-two-player: rgba(157, 0, 255, 0.04);

            --border-advanced: #b2b2b2;      /* Grey */
            --bg-advanced: rgba(178, 178, 178, 0.04);
        }

        :root[data-theme="light"] {
            /* Base Platform Architecture Overrides */
            --bg-main: #f4f5f7;
            --bg-card: #ffffff;
            --bg-main-box: #f9fafb;
            --text-primary: #111216;
            --text-secondary: #1f2937;
            --text-muted: #4b5563;
            --text-divider: #d1d5db;
            --color-link: #1d4ed8;

            /* --- LIGHT MODE ACCESSIBILITY CONTRAST OVERRIDES --- */
            /* Typography Overrides (Deepened values to ensure AAA text contrast on white panels) */
            --color-card-title: #0000ff;     /* Solid True Blue */
            --color-card-class: #00807b;     /* Deepened Cyan-Teal for text legibility */

            /* Callout Box Overrides (Enhanced background presence, darkened border text-hues) */
            --border-tip: #2c7a00;           /* Forest Green contrast anchor */
            --bg-tip: rgba(44, 122, 0, 0.06);

            --border-note: #058225;          /* Rich Foliage Green */
            --bg-note: rgba(5, 130, 37, 0.06);

            --border-example: #b58900;       /* High-contrast Amber instead of blinding neon yellow */
            --bg-example: rgba(181, 137, 0, 0.06);

            --border-discards: #c2410c;      /* Rust Orange */
            --bg-discards: rgba(194, 65, 12, 0.06);

            --border-challenge: #7c4623;     /* Earth Brown */
            --bg-challenge: rgba(124, 70, 35, 0.06);

            --border-important: #5c300f;     /* Deep Mahogany Brown */
            --bg-important: rgba(92, 48, 15, 0.06);

            --border-restriction: #b91c1c;   /* Deep Crimson Red */
            --bg-restriction: rgba(185, 28, 28, 0.06);

            --border-compatibility: #db2777; /* Deep Rose Pink for text validation readability */
            --bg-compatibility: rgba(219, 39, 119, 0.06);

            --border-victory: #6d28d9;       /* Deep Royal Purple */
            --bg-victory: rgba(109, 40, 217, 0.06);

            --border-two-player: #580096;    /* Dark Orchid Purple */
            --bg-two-player: rgba(88, 0, 150, 0.06);

            --border-advanced: #4b5563;      /* Dark Slate Slate Grey */
            --bg-advanced: rgba(75, 85, 99, 0.06);
        }
		
        /* ==========================================================================
           2. BASE LAYOUT CONFIGURATION & RESETS
           ========================================================================== */
        body {
            font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
            background-color: var(--bg-main);
            color: var(--text-secondary);
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
            line-height: 1.7;
            transition: background 0.3s, color 0.3s;
        }

        /* ==========================================================================
           3. AUTOMATED BREAKPOINT SENSOR ENGINE (TABLETS & WIDESCREENS)
           ========================================================================== */
        @media screen and (min-width: 768px) and (orientation: landscape) {
            body {
                max-width: 960px;
                margin: 40px auto;
                padding: 0 30px;
            }
            .rules-box {
                padding: 32px;
                margin: 24px 0;
            }
        }

        @media screen and (min-width: 1024px) {
            body {
                max-width: 1050px;
            }
        }

        /* ==========================================================================
           4. UNIFIED STRUCTURAL TYPOGRAPHY BLOCKS
           ========================================================================== */
        /* Main Page Header Component */
        .page-title-header {
            border-bottom: 3px double var(--text-divider);
            padding-bottom: 20px;
            margin-bottom: 40px;
        }
        h1.page-title {
            font-size: 2.5rem;
            color: var(--text-primary);
            margin: 0 0 5px 0;
            font-weight: 800;
            letter-spacing: -0.03em;
        }
        .meta-tag {
            color: var(--text-muted);
            font-size: 0.95rem;
            margin: 0;
            font-weight: 600;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.05em;
        }

        /* Expansion/Chapter Level Headings */
        h2.rulebook-heading {
            font-size: 1.6rem;
            color: var(--text-primary);
            margin-top: 40px;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
            border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent-heading);
            padding-bottom: 8px;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-transform: uppercase;
        }

        /* Operational Subheaders */
        h3.rulebook-subheading {
            font-size: 1.25rem;
            color: var(--text-secondary);
            margin-top: 25px;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
            border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-subheading);
            padding-left: 12px;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        /* Individual Card Entries Header Block */
        .card-header-block {
            border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--text-divider);
            padding-bottom: 8px;
            margin-bottom: 5px;
        }
        h4.card-title {
            font-size: 1.35rem;
            color: var(--text-primary);
            margin: 0;
            font-weight: 700;
            letter-spacing: -0.01em;
        }
        .card-class-info {
            font-size: 0.88rem;
            color: var(--accent-card-title);
            font-weight: 600;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.02em;
            margin-top: 2px;
        }

        /* Paragraphs and Core List Formats */
        p { color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 16px 0; }
        ul, ol { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; color: var(--text-secondary); }
        li { margin-bottom: 8px; }

        /* ==========================================================================
           5. DECOUPLED STRUCTURAL BLOCKS & BOX ARCHITECTURE
           ========================================================================== */
        .rules-box {
            background: var(--bg-card);
            border: 1px solid var(--text-divider);
            padding: 24px;
            border-radius: 12px;
            margin: 20px 0;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            gap: 15px;
        }

        /* Uniform Spacing Flow Override Module for Inside Elements */
        .rules-box > * {
            margin: 10px 0;
        }
        .rules-box > ul, .rules-box > ol {
            margin: 10px 0 10px 20px;
        }

        /* ==========================================================================
           6. MULTI-COLORED SEMANTIC CALLOUT ENGINE
           ========================================================================== */
        /* Shared Callout Box Core Parameters */
        .tip-box, .note-box, .example-box, .discards-box, .challenge-box, 
        .important-box, .alert-box, .compatibility-box, .victory-box, 
        .player-note-box, .advanced-box {
            font-size: 0.92rem;
            padding: 14px 16px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            color: var(--text-secondary);
            margin: 0; /* Keeps box alignment snug inside the parent flex gaps */
            font-weight: 500;
        }

        /* 🟢 1. TIPS CONTAINER (Light Green) */
        .tip-box {
            background: var(--bg-tip);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--border-tip);
        }

        /* 🟢 2. GENERAL NOTES CONTAINER (Green) */
        .note-box {
            background: var(--bg-note);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--border-note);
        }

        /* 🟢 3. METAGAME RULES EXAMPLES CONTAINER (Yellow) */
        .example-box {
            background: var(--bg-example);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--border-example);
            font-style: italic;
        }

        /* 🟢 4. DISCARDS POSITIONING ACTIONS CONTAINER (Orange) */
        .discards-box {
            background: var(--bg-discards);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--border-discards);
        }

        /* 🟢 5. CHALLENGE SYSTEM NOTES CONTAINER (Light Brown) */
        .challenge-box {
            background: var(--bg-challenge);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--border-challenge);
        }

        /* 🟢 6. CRITICAL METAGAME INFORMATION CONTAINER (Dark Brown) */
        .important-box {
            background: var(--bg-important);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--border-important);
        }

        /* 🟢 7. RESTRICTIONS & ILLEGAL PLAY PROTECTIONS CONTAINER (Red) */
        .alert-box {
            background: var(--bg-restriction);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--border-restriction);
        }

        /* 🟢 8. COMPATIBILITY & SEQUENCE NOTES CONTAINER (Pink) */
        .compatibility-box {
            background: var(--bg-compatibility);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--border-compatibility);
        }

        /* 🟢 9. SPECIAL VICTORY ENGINE CONDITIONS CONTAINER (Light Purple) */
        .victory-box {
            background: var(--bg-victory);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--border-victory);
        }

        /* 🟢 10. TWO-PLAYER BALANCE VARIATION MODULES CONTAINER (Purple) */
        .player-note-box {
            background: var(--bg-two-player);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--border-two-player);
        }

        /* 🟢 11. ADVANCED OPTIONAL HOUSE MODIFIERS CONTAINER (Grey) */
        .advanced-box {
            background: var(--bg-advanced);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--border-advanced);
        }

        /* ==========================================================================
           7. UNIFIED NAVIGATION LINKS & JUMP MATRIX INTERACTION
           ========================================================================== */
        /* Global Navigation Control Elements */
        .platform-hub-nav {
            margin-bottom: 25px;
        }
        .hub-link-button,
        .hub-link-button:visited,
        .hub-link-button:link {
            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            background: var(--bg-main-box);
            border: 1px solid var(--text-divider);
            color: var(--color-link) !important;
            padding: 10px 18px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: 700;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            transition: all 0.2s ease-in-out;
        }
        .hub-link-button:hover {
            background: var(--text-divider);
            color: var(--text-primary);
            transform: translateY(-1px);
        }

        /* Index Jump Matrix Table Container */
        .matrix-toc-box {
            background: var(--bg-card);
            border: 1px solid var(--text-divider);
            padding: 24px;
            border-radius: 12px;
            margin: 30px 0;
        }
        .matrix-toc-title {
            margin: 0 0 15px 0;
            color: var(--color-link);
            font-size: 1.15rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.02em;
        }
        .matrix-toc-grid {
            list-style: none;
            padding: 0;
            margin: 0;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            gap: 12px;
        }
		
		/* Hierarchical Indentation Modifiers inside the Matrix Grid */
        .matrix-item-heading { padding-left: 0px; font-weight: 700; }
        .matrix-item-subheading { padding-left: 15px; font-weight: 600; }
        .matrix-item-card { padding-left: 30px; font-weight: 500; font-style: italic; }

        .matrix-link {
            color: var(--text-muted);
            text-decoration: none;
            transition: color 0.15s;
        }
        .matrix-link:hover {
            color: var(--color-link);
            text-decoration: underline;
        }

        /* Bottom Step Jump Elements */
        .return-link-wrapper {
            text-align: right;
            margin-top: -5px;
            margin-bottom: 35px;
        }
        .return-link,
        .return-link:visited,
        .return-link:link {
            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            background: var(--bg-main-box);
            border: 1px solid var(--text-divider);
            color: var(--color-link) !important; /* Forces your exact brand link colour */
            padding: 8px 14px; /* Clean, slightly tighter padding for the bottom link */
            border-radius: 8px;
            text-decoration: none;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            transition: all 0.2s ease-in-out;
        }

        .return-link:hover {
            background: var(--text-divider);
            color: var(--text-primary) !important;
            transform: translateY(-1px);
            text-decoration: none;
        }

        /* ==========================================================================
           8. UNIFIED MEDIA ENGINE & VISUAL CARD GRIDS
           ========================================================================== */
        .image-container {
            margin: 20px auto;
            padding: 12px;
            background: var(--bg-main-box);
            border: 1px solid var(--text-divider);
            border-radius: 8px;
            text-align: center;
            max-width: 100%;
        }
        .image-container img {
            max-width: 100%;
            max-height: 450px;
            width: auto;
            height: auto;
            object-fit: contain;
            border-radius: 6px;
            display: inline-block; /* Allows images to sit side-by-side */
            margin: 5px; /* Adds a little breathing room between them */
            border: 1px solid var(--text-divider);
        }
        .image-caption {
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            margin-top: 10px;
            font-weight: 500;
            line-height: 1.4;
        }

        /* Horizontal Layout Row Wrapper (Flex Grid Modifiers) */
        .image-row-container {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            gap: 15px;
            justify-content: center;
            margin: 20px 0;
            width: 100%;
        }
        .image-row-container .image-container {
            flex: 1 1 calc(33.333% - 15px);
            min-width: 220px;
            margin: 0;
        }

        /* Border Color Coatings for Core and Extension Cards */
        .image-container.border-steel { border: 3px solid #1d4ed8; }
        .image-container.border-poison-core { border: 3px solid #6b21a8; }
        .image-container.border-venom-core { border: 3px solid #dc2626; }
        .image-container.border-carbon { border: 3px solid #ea580c; }
        .image-container.border-stinger-core { border: 3px solid #eab308; }
        .image-container.border-toxin-core { border: 3px solid #16a34a; }
        .image-container.border-diamond { border: 3px solid #3b82f6; }
        .image-container.border-emerald { border: 3px solid #10b981; }
        .image-container.border-redwood { border: 3px solid #5c4033; }
        .image-container.border-oak { border: 3px solid #b58900; }
        .image-container.border-rose { border: 3px solid #ec4899; }
        .image-container.border-amethyst { border: 3px solid #8b5cf6; }
        .image-container.border-stone { border: 3px solid #6b7280; }
		
		/* ==========================================================================
           10. EXPANSION CONTENT GRID ARCHITECTURE
           ========================================================================== */
        .expansion-grid {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            gap: 12px;
            width: 100%;
            margin: 15px 0;
        }

        .expansion-row {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column; /* Stacks name and description cleanly on mobile screens */
            justify-content: space-between;
            padding: 10px 14px;
            background: var(--bg-main-box);
            border: 1px solid var(--text-divider);
            border-radius: 8px;
            gap: 4px;
        }

        .expansion-name {
            font-weight: 700;
            color: var(--text-primary);
            font-size: 0.95rem;
        }

        .expansion-desc {
            font-weight: 500;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            font-size: 0.9rem;
        }

        /* Responsive Side-by-Side Split Modifier for Widescreen Monitors */
        @media screen and (min-width: 600px) {
            .expansion-row {
                flex-direction: row; /* Converts back to a horizontal split line once space allows */
                align-items: center;
                gap: 15px;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body id="top">

    <nav class="platform-hub-nav" aria-label="Platform Navigation">
        <a href="/" class="hub-link-button">📂 Return to Rulebook Hub</a>
    </nav>

    <h1>[00] SOLOVERSE - CRAZY 8’s [TUTORIAL RULEBOOK] [START HERE]</h1>
    <div class="meta-tag">👥 Ages 7+, 3-6 Players • v1.0.0</div>

    <!-- INDEX JUMP MATRIX -->
    <nav class="matrix-toc-box" aria-label="Rulebook Table of Contents Matrix">
        <h2 class="matrix-toc-title">📋 RULEBOOK CONTENTS</h2>
        <ul class="matrix-toc-grid">
			<li class="matrix-item-heading">
				<a href="#object" class="matrix-link">OBJECT</a>
			</li>
            <li class="matrix-item-heading">
				<a href="#setup" class="matrix-link">SETUP</a>
			</li>
            <li class="matrix-item-heading">
				<a href="#how-to-play" class="matrix-link">HOW TO PLAY</a>
			</li>
            <li class="matrix-item-heading">
				<a href="#victory-conditions" class="matrix-link">VICTORY CONDITIONS</a>
			</li>
        </ul>
    </nav>

    <!-- OBJECT -->
	<div id="object">
		<div class="rules-box">
			<h4>OBJECT</h4>
			<ul>
				<li>This game follows the Crazy 8’s style of “Card Shedding” play [You might be reminded of other Hand Shedding Card Games].</li>
				<li>Therefore: Be the first Player to get rid of all your Cards.</li>
			</ul>
			<div class="return-link-wrapper">
				<a href="#top" class="return-link">🔝 Return to Rulebook Contents</a>
			</div>
		</div>
    </div>
	
    <!-- SETUP -->
	<div id="setup">
		<div class="rules-box">
			<h4>SETUP</h4>
            <ol>
                <li>For this Tutorial Game, please choose and separate any 4 Colours in the Game. Each Colour Set contains 26 Cards, including 2 Copies of each of the following:
                    <ol type="i">
                        <li>The Numbers 0-9.</li>
                        <li>Draw +2 [Action. The Next Player must Draw 2 Cards and Skip Their Turn. And Yes You can Stack a Draw +2 on another].
                            <div class="image-container">
                        	    <div class="image-caption">Image 1: Draw +2.</div>
                                    <img src="/assets/images/cards/000-1-steel-draw-2.png">
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>Reverse [Action. The Direction of Play Reverses (Remember to Flip the <strong>Direction of Play</strong> Setup Card) ].
                            <div class="image-container">
                                <div class="image-caption">Image 2: Reverse.</div>
                                    <img src="/assets/images/cards/000-12-poison-reverse.png">
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>Skip [Action. The Next Player's Turn is Skipped].
                            <div class="image-container">
                            	<div class="image-caption">Image 3: Skip.</div>
                                    <img src="/assets/images/cards/000-9-venom-skip.png">
                            </div>
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                </li>
                <li>Next, separate the following Chaos Cards [Black & White] for the best Tutorial experience:
                    <ol type="i">
                        <li>2 x Pure Chaos [Simply Changes the Colour].
                            <div class="image-container">
                            	<div class="image-caption">Image 4: Pure Chaos.</div>
                                    <img src="/assets/images/cards/00-core-game-pure-chaos.png">
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>2 x Pure Chaos [Reverse] [Reverses Play, then Changes the Colour; the Previous Player is also allowed to match the Reverse Symbol, not just the Colour called].
                            <div class="image-container">
                                <div class="image-caption">Image 5: Pure Chaos Reverse.</div>
                                    <img src="/assets/images/cards/00-core-game-pure-chaos-reverse.png">
                                </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>2 x Pure Chaos [Skip] [Skips the Next Player, then Changes the Colour; the following Player is also allowed to match the Skip Symbol, not just the Colour called].
                            <div class="image-container">
                                <div class="image-caption">Image 6: Pure Chaos Skip.</div>
                                    <img src="/assets/images/cards/00-core-game-pure-chaos-skip.png">
                                </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>1 x Pure Chaos [Shuffle Hands] [The User collects all Player's Cards, Shuffles them and Re-Deals them as equally to all Players. Then Changes the Colour].
                            <div class="image-container">
                                <div class="image-caption">Image 7: Pure Chaos Shuffle Hands.</div>
                                    <img src="/assets/images/cards/00-core-game-pure-chaos-shuffle-hands.png">
                                </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>2 x Chaos Draw +4 [For the Tutorial, the Next Player must either: Draw 4 Cards or Respond in Kind by Stacking any other Chaos Draw +4 or Counter it with NOU. You can only Play them if You do NOT have any Matching Coloured Card that is Playable or Responding in Kind. Finally, Change the Colour].
                            <div class="image-container">
                                <div class="image-caption">Image 7: Chaos Draw +4.</div>
                                    <img src="/assets/images/cards/00-core-game-chaos-draw-4.png">
                                </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>2 x Chaos Draw +4 [Reverse] [For the Tutorial, first Reverse Play from the User, and the Previous Player must either: Draw 4 Cards or Respond in Kind by Stacking any other Chaos Draw +4 or Counter it with NOU. You can only Play them if You do NOT have any Matching Coloured Card that is Playable or Responding in Kind (Stacking or Countering). Finally, once the Draw is resolved, anyone is also allowed to match the Reverse Symbol, not just the Colour called. Finally, Change the Colour].
                            <div class="image-container">
                                <div class="image-caption">Image 8: Chaos Draw +4 [Reverse].</div>
                                    <img src="/assets/images/cards/00-core-game-chaos-draw-4-reverse.png">
                                </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>2 x Chaos Draw +4 [Skip] [For the Tutorial, first Skip the Next Player, then the following Player must either: Draw 4 Cards orRespond in Kind by Stacking any other Chaos Draw +4 or Counter it with NOU. You can only Play them if You do NOT have any Matching Coloured Card that is Playable or Responding in Kind. Finally, once the Draw is resolved, anyone is also allowed to match the Reverse Symbol, not just the Colour called. Finally, Change the Colour].
                            <div class="image-container">
                                <div class="image-caption">Image 9: Chaos Draw +4 Skip.</div>
                                    <img src="/assets/images/cards/00-core-game-chaos-draw-4-skip.png">
                                </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>2 x Anti-Fun [Optional Counter LV1 Effect: Play on another Player's Turn when they Play Their last Card to Win. Cancel that Win and force Them to Deal 5 New Cards to Themselves, finally Change the Colour. Or Play as a Pure Chaos Card and simply Change the Colour].
                            <div class="image-container">
                                <div class="image-caption">Image 10: Anti-Fun.</div>
                                    <img src="/assets/images/cards/00-core-game-counter-lv1-anti-fun.png">
                                </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>2 x NOU [A Counter LV2 Chaos Card. Reflect a Chaos Draw +4 back at it's User, then Reverse Play from them. Optionally, Play Last as a Pure Chaos Card and Change the Colour to Pre-Counter Anti-Fun and experience the Official Undefeatable Victory!].
                            <div class="image-container">
                                <div class="image-caption">Image 11: NOU.</div>
                                    <img src="/assets/images/cards/00-core-game-counter-lv2-nou.png">
                                </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>2 x Clone [Copies the Previous Card on the Discards - Follow it's Rules, if any].
                            <div class="image-container">
                                <div class="image-caption">Image 12: Clone.</div>
                                    <img src="/assets/images/cards/00-core-game-clone.png">
                                </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>2 x Stun [Target any Player at the Table and Play in Front of Them. When Their next PLAYABLE TURN arrives, it is automatically Skipped. Then the Targeted Player Changes the Colour. The Following Player is also allowed to match the Skip Symbol, not just the Colour called].
                            <div class="image-container">
                                <div class="image-caption">Image 14: Stun.</div>
                                    <img src="/assets/images/cards/00-core-game-stun.png">
                                </div>
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                </li>
                <li>Choose who Deals first [alternate the Dealer clockwise after each game].</li>
				<li>Shuffle the Deck, then the Dealer Deals Each Player 1 Card at a time until all have 7 Cards face-down [watch out for the face-up Trap Class Chaos Cards – return them randomly to the Deck before continuing to Deal].</li>
				<li>Place the remainder of the Cards face-down as a Deck.</li>
				<li>Place the <strong>Direction Of Play [Blue/Clockwise Side]</strong> and the <strong>Play To The Side Of The Discards</strong> Setup Cards face-up on either side of the Discards, where everyone can see them [Remember to Flip the <strong>Direction Of Play</strong> Setup Card it every time a Reverse Effect Activates].</li>
				<li>Flip the top Card of the Deck over to begin the Discards:
					<ol type="a">
						<li>If any Action Class Cards are turned over at this stage, follow their rules.</li>
						<li>If any Chaos Card is turned over [including if a Trap Class Chaos Card is revealed in doing so], return it randomly to the Deck and Flip another Card.</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<div class="return-link-wrapper">
				<a href="#top" class="return-link">🔝 Return to Rulebook Contents</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
	
